                env.close();

It would be nice to add a comment about what this lambda does.  Perhaps something like...
```
            // lambda that returns the JSON form of NFTokens held by acct
```
You also don't need any captures.  All the relevant information is passed in.  But, since we're talking about captures, it makes more sense to me to capture `env`, rather than pass it in.  It reduces noise at the call sites.  So I'd be inclined to make the signature of the lambda look like this:
```
            // lambda that returns the JSON form of NFTokens held by acct
            auto accountNFTs = [&env](Account const& acct) {
```

